# Normalize line endings to LF in the repository AND in the working copy.
# Development happens on Windows (core.autocrlf=true) while the GitHub Actions
# runner is Linux — without this, Prettier and ESLint would disagree about line
# endings between the two environments.
* text=auto eol=lf

# The research document is versioned directly in Git (no Git LFS — ~3MB does not
# justify the extra tooling). Mark it binary so Git never tries to diff or
# normalize its contents.
*.docx binary
